WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:04.790
Producers Phil Lord and Christopher Miller
have said the Lego Batman Movie is one giant

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:07.280
easter egg for Batman aficionados.

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:12.420
And the film really is totally packed with
DC comics, movie and TV easter eggs, in-jokes

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:13.420
and references.

00:00:13.420 --> 00:00:16.740
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here,
and in this video, I'm going to take a look

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:19.990
at all the best easter eggs and references
I spotted in the movie.

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:24.279
I'm also giving away this awesome pair of
LEGO Batman Movie books; that's The Essential

00:00:24.279 --> 00:00:28.900
Guide plus this very cool Making Of the movie,
which is stuffed with concept art, sketches

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:30.110
and LEGO builds.

00:00:30.110 --> 00:00:34.079
For a chance to win, make sure you subscribe
and leave a comment on this video about your

00:00:34.079 --> 00:00:36.480
favourite easter egg or any I missed.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:39.930
Just before I start, quick warning: there
are spoilers ahead, so if you're not ready

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:43.760
for those, hail your nearest Batmobile outta
here by tapping or clicking the screen for

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:45.809
my spoiler-free review of the movie.

00:00:45.809 --> 00:00:50.280
Let's start with Harley Quinn, who has the
word "Smylex" written on the front of her

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:54.290
costume, which is an easter egg to the poison
the Joker used to terrorise Gotham in the

00:00:54.290 --> 00:00:56.199
1989 Batman movie.

00:00:56.199 --> 00:01:00.739
In that film, Jack Nicholson's Joker laced
various products throughout Gotham with Smylex

00:01:00.739 --> 00:01:05.220
which would cause victims to laugh uncontrollably
until they died with a frozen grin on their

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:06.350
face.

00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:10.530
And when Pilot Bill reminds the Joker that
Batman has always foiled his plans like that

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:14.560
time with the Prince music and the parade,
it's another hat tip to that first Batman

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:18.750
movie by Tim Burton, where the Joker plays
Prince music during the parade he organised

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:23.090
to offer free cash to the citizens of Gotham
while secretly planning to unleash Smylex

00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:24.560
gas on everyone.

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:30.040
There's another reference to the 1989 Batman
movie when Lego Batman says, "let's get nuts"

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:34.509
after the Joker challenges him at the Gotham
Energy Facility, which echoes the time Michael

00:01:34.509 --> 00:01:39.259
Keaton's Bruce Wayne flew into a rage with
the Joker in the '89 Batman movie and said

00:01:39.259 --> 00:01:41.200
those same words.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:45.259
The Dark Knight movie also gets referenced
by the pilot when he reminds the Clown Prince

00:01:45.259 --> 00:01:48.159
of Crime about "that time with the two boats".

00:01:48.159 --> 00:01:52.310
What he's talking about is the dilemma that
Heath Ledger's Joker set up in that movie

00:01:52.310 --> 00:01:56.310
when he loaded two ferries with explosives,
offering each boat the choice to blow the

00:01:56.310 --> 00:01:59.110
other up or both be destroyed.

00:01:59.110 --> 00:02:02.450
And it was a brilliant bit of meta-humour
when the pilots requesting permission to fly

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:07.759
over the most crime-ridden city in the world
with a plane packed with explosives were working

00:02:07.759 --> 00:02:10.620
for none other than MacGuffin Airlines!

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:15.300
The movie also references Batman's origins
via a family photo outside the Monarch Theatre

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:19.140
that Bruce Wayne and his parents visited on
the night that his parents were murdered.

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:23.280
The streets of Lego Gotham are also littered
with easter eggs hidden in building names

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:24.640
and billboards.

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:28.780
First up is the Iceberg Lounge, a nightclub
from the comics that's run by the Penguin

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:31.670
and used as a front for his illegal activities.

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:35.590
The Big Belly Burger chain also operates in
Lego Batman's Gotham.

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:39.880
Big Belly Burger has featured regularly in
the Arrow and The Flash TV shows and first

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:43.430
appeared in the Adventures of Superman comic
book series in 1988.

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:48.450
Another sign on a building is the name Magnus
which could be a nod to the comic book character

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:53.140
Will Magnus, a genius robotic scientist and
creator of the Metal Men.

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:56.840
When Superman is being interviewed on TV,
people are watching the programme outside

00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:59.150
a store called Wendell's Electronics.

00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:03.400
In the comics, Wendell Lewis was the Sewer
King and operated a criminal underworld in

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:05.150
Gotham's sewers.

00:03:05.150 --> 00:03:09.930
And during that Gotham City News TV broadcast,
Man of Steel director Zach Synder gets a visual

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:14.480
shout-out when the footage being shown is
credited as "courtesy of Zach Snyder and A.

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:15.480
Mokri".

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:18.100
Amir Mokri by the way was the cinematographer
for Man of Steel.

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:23.780
Among the movies showing at the cinema in
Gotham is one called Two Shades of Grey, a

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:27.890
joke and reference to the fact that the Fifty
Shades of Grey movie sequel, Fifty Shades

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:32.260
Darker, is released in cinemas on the same
day as The Lego Batman Movie.

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:36.310
Gotham's sister city Blüdhaven gets referenced
in The Lego Batman Movie and there's a clever

00:03:36.310 --> 00:03:40.120
double easter egg and joke in the name of
the Bludhound Express bus.

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:45.180
Bludhound is not only a word-play on the Greyhound
bus line, but it's also a nod to the DC Comics

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:51.430
intergalactic criminal Bludhound, and possibly
also to Bludhaven's baseball team: the Bloodhounds.

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:56.090
The ad for Lazlo's ham with a picture of a
butcher wearing a pig's mask is a nice reference

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:59.620
to Lazlo Valentin, aka Professor Pyg from
the comics.

00:03:59.620 --> 00:04:04.250
Professor Pyg is a particularly unhinged Batman
villain who's obsessed with trying to make

00:04:04.250 --> 00:04:05.730
people perfect.

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:10.120
In the movie, the Joker also hijacks one of
Lazlo's Slaughterhouse trucks to break into

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:11.670
the Gotham power plant, renaming it Joker's
Laughter Truck.

00:04:11.670 --> 00:04:16.030
There's also a billboard for Zesti Cola, one
of the two big soda drink manufacturers in

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:17.970
the DC Comics universe.

00:04:17.970 --> 00:04:22.640
And Zesti's main rival, Soder Cola, also pops
up later on another billboard.

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:26.930
There's a tiny little ad for Kessel Coffee
on the top of a yellow cab, a reference to

00:04:26.930 --> 00:04:29.570
the DC Comics writer and inker Karl Kessel.

00:04:29.570 --> 00:04:34.500
Kessel worked on numerous Superman titles
and created the modern version of Superboy.

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:38.840
And there's also a sign for Shondra's, which
could be an easter egg to metahuman Shondra

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:42.570
Kinsolving's clinic which Bruce Wayne attended
in the comics.

00:04:42.570 --> 00:04:46.900
Teen band The Flips, who've appeared in a
number of Teen Titans comics, show up on a

00:04:46.900 --> 00:04:48.340
billboard in Gotham City.

00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:53.980
Ferris Air, the aviation company that employs
Hal Jordan, aka Green Lantern, appears numerous

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:55.430
times in the movie.

00:04:55.430 --> 00:04:59.540
There are billboards and ads for the company
throughout Gotham as well as Ferris Air aeroplanes

00:04:59.540 --> 00:05:00.850
at the airport.

00:05:00.850 --> 00:05:05.220
The villain Plastique seems to have her own
perfume range in the Lego universe with a

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:06.810
billboard for Plastique Parfum!

00:05:06.810 --> 00:05:12.500
There's also a nice wink to the upcoming Lego
Ninjago Movie via the billboard for "Ninjagotown."

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:17.850
The name and design is also a very cool homage
to the 1974 movie Chinatown which, of course,

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:22.000
starred Jack Nicholson, the Joker in 1989's
Batman.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:27.960
Batman also carries a pair of Ninjago Jadeblades
which have appeared on Lego's Ninjago TV series.

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:32.170
And Batman's excessive utility belt, which
has been poked fun at over the years, gets

00:05:32.170 --> 00:05:36.530
a funny moment when he unloads it before going
through Arkham Asylum's security system.

00:05:36.530 --> 00:05:42.860
As well as a huge utility belt, Lego Batman
also has a huge ego which extends to a rivalry

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:47.660
with Iron Man, perhaps one of his greatest
current cinematic rivals, both being billionaire,

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:52.150
playboy, philanthropists with a shed-load
of high-tech gear at their disposal.

00:05:52.150 --> 00:05:56.930
Hilariously, the password for access to the
Batcave is none other than "Iron Man Sucks".

00:05:56.930 --> 00:06:01.930
There's a few times in the movie when Batman
refers to Bruce Wayne as Bruno rather than

00:06:01.930 --> 00:06:05.900
Bruce, which is a nod to how, in numerous
Spanish-speaking countries, Bruce Wayne is

00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:08.860
actually called Bruno Diaz.

00:06:08.860 --> 00:06:13.210
As you'd expect, the Batcave is filled to
bursting with easter eggs, references, and

00:06:13.210 --> 00:06:14.210
jokes.

00:06:14.210 --> 00:06:18.240
Starting with the batsuits, White Bat is Batman's
camouflaged batsuit from the comics that he's

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:20.710
used in snowy places like the North Pole.

00:06:20.710 --> 00:06:24.450
Tears of a Bat is a pun on Smokey Robison's
song Tears of a Clown.

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:29.220
And Bat By Gaslight is a nod to the single
issue comic book Gotham by Gaslight.

00:06:29.220 --> 00:06:34.380
Krampus Bat is a play on the half-demon half-goat
mythological figure that punishes badly-behaved

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:36.650
children around Christmas time.

00:06:36.650 --> 00:06:41.120
Raging Bat comes complete with boxing gloves
and is a reference to Martin Scorsese's Oscar-winning

00:06:41.120 --> 00:06:44.670
movie Raging Bull, starring Robert De Niro
as the boxer Jake LaMotta.

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:49.061
And the Night Terror suit is likely a nod
to the Batman Knight Terrors series in The

00:06:49.061 --> 00:06:50.590
New 52.

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:55.230
The Batcave is also full of Batman's crazy
vehicles including the Bat-Sub, the Bat Space

00:06:55.230 --> 00:06:59.480
Shuttle, the Bat Zeppelin, the Bat Train,
the Bat Kayak and the Bat Dune Buggy.

00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:04.080
There are stacks of Batmobiles in the Batcave
and there's an easter egg to Batmobile designer

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:07.990
George Barris via the ad for Barris Automotives
on the back of the Brick!

00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:11.370
magazine that Bruce Wayne pulls out at the
police gala event.

00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:15.500
George Barris created the first design of
the 60s TV show Batmobile.

00:07:15.500 --> 00:07:18.210
The Bat Garage also includes some crafty easter
eggs.

00:07:18.210 --> 00:07:22.550
For example, there's a plaque for the Ovel
Oil company which sponsored the comic book

00:07:22.550 --> 00:07:23.820
superhero team The Conglomerate.

00:07:23.820 --> 00:07:29.200
And there's a funny moment in the Batcave
when Dick Grayson spots the Bat Shark Repellent

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:31.400
which Batman says is completely useless.

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:36.880
It's a little joke about the Shark Repellent
Bat Spray from the 1966 Batman movie.

00:07:36.880 --> 00:07:40.881
The shark repellent from that movie has been
lampooned many times, however, later in The

00:07:40.881 --> 00:07:46.140
Lego Batman Movie the spray does actually
work when Lego Jaws attacks Batman.

00:07:46.140 --> 00:07:51.449
And the 1960s Batman TV show gets tons of
fun references, homages, and jokes all the

00:07:51.449 --> 00:07:53.010
way through Lego Batman.

00:07:53.010 --> 00:07:57.870
The iconic theme tune is referenced throughout,
for example Lego Batman's opening song "Who's

00:07:57.870 --> 00:07:58.870
the Batman?"

00:07:58.870 --> 00:07:59.870
has the "Batman!"

00:07:59.870 --> 00:08:04.750
refrain sung by the backing singers as well
as the repeated line "Na na na na na na Batman!".

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:09.060
And there's more riffs later on, for example,
when Batman refuses to go to the police gala

00:08:09.060 --> 00:08:11.240
with a string of "no no no no no no-s".

00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:16.389
I also loved hearing Batman say "To the batmobile"
with Robin responding "Hot Diggidy Dog!"

00:08:16.389 --> 00:08:20.980
followed up with a Lego version of the TV
show's Bat logo scene transition.

00:08:20.980 --> 00:08:26.030
Robin's cheesy "Holy Batman" phrases from
the TV show also get a nod with Robin's "Holy

00:08:26.030 --> 00:08:30.740
family photo" after his selfie with Batman,
Batgirl and Alfred.

00:08:30.740 --> 00:08:34.950
The Bat-Fight words from the 60s show and
movie also pop up as Batman and Robin say

00:08:34.950 --> 00:08:39.930
they're going to 'hit the bad guys so hard
it will make words appear on the screen'.

00:08:39.930 --> 00:08:44.430
And when Alfred puts on a Lego version of
Adam West's blue and grey Batsuit he says

00:08:44.430 --> 00:08:46.860
it's because he misses the 60s.

00:08:46.860 --> 00:08:51.020
Later, Alfred reveals that he used to be a
tail gunner, which is a nod to both the time

00:08:51.020 --> 00:08:55.410
he served in the Royal Air Force in the comics
and also to the fact that Alfred in the upcoming

00:08:55.410 --> 00:08:59.060
Justice League movie will be a tail gunner
on the Flying Fox.

00:08:59.060 --> 00:09:03.390
By the way, when Alfred and Robin have to
take out the Gremlins trying to destroy their

00:09:03.390 --> 00:09:08.080
craft, it's a hat tip to the origin of the
word "gremlin" in RAF pilot slang as the pilots

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:12.520
attributed faults in their planes to impish
little creatures that sabotaged aircraft (and

00:09:12.520 --> 00:09:14.120
who they called gremlins).

00:09:14.120 --> 00:09:18.310
Barbara Gordon also references many of the
major moments in Batman's lengthy history

00:09:18.310 --> 00:09:22.390
when she says in her speech that Batman's
been on the job a very long time.

00:09:22.390 --> 00:09:27.540
A series of pictures from all the major Batman
films show up, including the 1940s serials

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:33.070
and also various iconic comic book covers
such as Frank Miller's The Dark Knight Returns.

00:09:33.070 --> 00:09:37.670
And Barbara Gordon herself gets a brand new
backstory in Lego Batman which the filmmakers

00:09:37.670 --> 00:09:41.640
have said "deviates from the DC canon to a
ridiculous degree".

00:09:41.640 --> 00:09:46.630
It turns out Barbara Gordon trained at Harvard
For Police and then cleaned up the crime-ridden

00:09:46.630 --> 00:09:48.580
Blüdhaven with statistics.

00:09:48.580 --> 00:09:53.420
To suit up Barbara Gordon as Batgirl, Batman
uses his Bat Merch gun, trying out a number

00:09:53.420 --> 00:09:54.630
of costumes on her.

00:09:54.630 --> 00:09:59.320
One of them is Bat Lady which could be a reference
to the fictional Bat Lady comic book character

00:09:59.320 --> 00:10:05.010
from the 1955 musical comedy Artists and Models
which starred Dean Martin and Jerry Lewis.

00:10:05.010 --> 00:10:08.950
The Bat Merch gun then hits Barbara Gordon
with a pink Batarina outfit and then a Soccer

00:10:08.950 --> 00:10:11.260
Mom costume both of which she hates.

00:10:11.260 --> 00:10:15.931
Eventually, she gets a cool costume that has
the feel of Yvonne Craig's costume from the

00:10:15.931 --> 00:10:17.440
60s TV series.

00:10:17.440 --> 00:10:21.680
The Lego Batman Movie also plays fast and
loose with the history of Batgirl's relationship

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:25.750
with Batman in the comics, with Batman saying
at the end of the movie that Batgirl is his

00:10:25.750 --> 00:10:27.760
platonic, co-worker buddy, who's a girl, but
just a friend.

00:10:27.760 --> 00:10:33.580
For the wonder boy Robin, there are plenty
of nods and easter eggs to his comic book

00:10:33.580 --> 00:10:35.040
and screen history.

00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:39.250
When Dick Grayson approaches Bruce Wayne to
ask what qualities will get him adopted, two

00:10:39.250 --> 00:10:42.320
which he mentions are cooking and gymnastic
abilities.

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:47.170
On the Teen Titans TV series, Dick Grayson
is a great sandwich maker, and his acrobatic

00:10:47.170 --> 00:10:51.710
skills and circus background are mentioned
in both the comics and on screen, for instance,

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:53.120
in Batman Forever.

00:10:53.120 --> 00:10:57.370
If you look closely, you'll also spot a line
of robins on Dick Grayson's jumper, a nice

00:10:57.370 --> 00:11:01.910
bit of detail ahead of his later suggestion
that he take on the superhero nickname of

00:11:01.910 --> 00:11:02.910
Robin.

00:11:02.910 --> 00:11:06.620
Robin's transformation into Nightwing later
in the movie, while Batman is stuck in the

00:11:06.620 --> 00:11:10.149
Phantom Zone, reflects how he grew out of
being Batman's sidekick in the comics and

00:11:10.149 --> 00:11:11.850
into that new role.

00:11:11.850 --> 00:11:16.339
Michael Cera, who plays Robin, also starred
alongside Lego Batman's Will Arnett in the

00:11:16.339 --> 00:11:20.450
TV comedy series Arrested Development and
there's a nice shout-out to Cera's character

00:11:20.450 --> 00:11:22.770
on that TV show, George Michael Bluth.

00:11:22.770 --> 00:11:26.820
When Robin suggests various superhero theme
songs, he plays Wham's Wake Me Up Before You

00:11:26.820 --> 00:11:31.560
Go Go which was written, produced and sung
by George Michael.

00:11:31.560 --> 00:11:35.300
One of the roles which Zach Galifianakis,
who voices the Joker, is most famous for is

00:11:35.300 --> 00:11:37.100
Alan in The Hangover movie trilogy.

00:11:37.100 --> 00:11:41.490
And there's a subtle nod to that character
when Robin kicks a guy just outside the Joker's

00:11:41.490 --> 00:11:44.680
cell in Arkham Asylum saying, "take that Alan!"

00:11:44.680 --> 00:11:49.300
Joel Schumacher's Batman Forever gets quite
a lot of shout-outs in The Lego Batman Movie,

00:11:49.300 --> 00:11:53.790
from fireworks, to a Batman Forever batsuit,
and a Batman Forever placard.

00:11:53.790 --> 00:11:57.890
And Christopher Nolan's Batman trilogy also
gets numerous references.

00:11:57.890 --> 00:12:02.180
For example, when Batman is doing a series
of push-ups while Alfred lectures him, it's

00:12:02.180 --> 00:12:06.630
very similar to when Alfred is lecturing Christian
Bale's Bruce Wayne while he's does push-ups

00:12:06.630 --> 00:12:08.399
in Batman Begins.

00:12:08.399 --> 00:12:11.890
And the reference to Bruce Wayne and Russian
ballerinas is a nod to the time in The Dark

00:12:11.890 --> 00:12:15.610
Knight when Bruce Wayne went off on a ship
with the Russian ballet as a cover for his

00:12:15.610 --> 00:12:18.470
planned operation in Hong Kong.

00:12:18.470 --> 00:12:22.500
Batgirl in Lego Batman tips her hat to the
brutal magic trick that Heath Ledger's Joker

00:12:22.500 --> 00:12:26.210
performed with a pencil when she says to Voldemort,
"Wanna see a magic trick?

00:12:26.210 --> 00:12:30.280
I'm gonna make you disappear" as she sends
him back to the Phantom Zone.

00:12:30.280 --> 00:12:34.080
And Bane in the movie not only sounds like
Tom Hardy's Bane from The Dark Knight Rises,

00:12:34.080 --> 00:12:39.400
but he also riffs on one of Bane's lines when
he cries, "we will be the Joker's reckoning!"

00:12:39.400 --> 00:12:43.580
By the way, the hijacking of MacGuffin Airlines
at the beginning of the movie has shades of

00:12:43.580 --> 00:12:47.610
the opening to The Dark Knight Rises where
Bane's henchmen hijack the plane where he's

00:12:47.610 --> 00:12:49.029
being held.

00:12:49.029 --> 00:12:53.290
The most recent live-action Batman movie was,
of course, Batman v Superman, and there are

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:55.630
some hilarious nods to that film.

00:12:55.630 --> 00:12:59.470
First up is the music during the opening titles,
which has a definite touch of the dramatic

00:12:59.470 --> 00:13:04.000
drum theme from BvS, as Batman pokes fun at
the various logos.

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:09.420
The Batman-Superman rivalry is played up when
the DC logo appears and Batman brags "DC – The

00:13:09.420 --> 00:13:10.970
House That Batman Built."

00:13:10.970 --> 00:13:16.080
And in the movie, Batman even taunts Superman
saying "come at me bro, I'm your kryptonite."

00:13:16.080 --> 00:13:20.360
There's also a funny flashback that is a Lego
recreation of the confrontation between Batman

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:22.610
and Superman in Dawn of Justice.

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:27.080
Despite this rivalry, Batman still ends up
paying Superman a visit as he needs to steal

00:13:27.080 --> 00:13:30.290
the Phantom Zone Projector from the Fortress
of Solitude.

00:13:30.290 --> 00:13:34.710
And there's a brilliant audio easter egg when
Batman rings Superman's doorbell and it plays

00:13:34.710 --> 00:13:37.360
the Superman theme by John Williams.

00:13:37.360 --> 00:13:40.940
If you were wondering about the large arrow
symbol on the entrance to the Fortress of

00:13:40.940 --> 00:13:45.490
Solitude, well it's a little joke about the
big arrow-shaped key that Superman has sometimes

00:13:45.490 --> 00:13:49.330
used to secure access to the Fortress of Solitude
in the comics.

00:13:49.330 --> 00:13:54.450
Once inside, Batman discovers Superman is
having a Justice League 57th Anniversary Party,

00:13:54.450 --> 00:13:59.890
a reference the fact that the Justice League
first appeared 57 years ago in 1960 in issue

00:13:59.890 --> 00:14:02.590
28 of The Brave And The Bold comic book.

00:14:02.590 --> 00:14:07.470
And when Batman takes a photo of the Justice
League they all say "Super Friends", a reference

00:14:07.470 --> 00:14:12.180
to the animated TV series that aired in the
1970s and 80s and which adapted the Justice

00:14:12.180 --> 00:14:13.800
League characters for TV.

00:14:13.800 --> 00:14:18.450
By the way, Wonder Dog, who DJs at the party,
has a green cape just like Wonder Dog from

00:14:18.450 --> 00:14:21.200
the Super Friends animated series.

00:14:21.200 --> 00:14:26.370
Inside the fortress, Batman accidentally activates
a hologram of Superman's father Jor-El in

00:14:26.370 --> 00:14:30.760
a hilarious moment as Batman just ignores
Jor-El's message about the crystals that he's

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:33.880
destroying containing irreplaceable knowledge.

00:14:33.880 --> 00:14:38.250
The Atomic Cauldron is a nod to the cauldron
which powers the Fortress in the comics.

00:14:38.250 --> 00:14:42.529
Batman has a jab at the recent Suicide Squad
movie when he scoffs at why he would use one

00:14:42.529 --> 00:14:44.720
group of criminals to defeat another group
of criminals.

00:14:44.720 --> 00:14:49.670
And there's a shout out to Harley Quinn's
alter ego, psychiatrist Dr Harleen Quinzel,

00:14:49.670 --> 00:14:55.190
on the Phantom's Own laundry truck which reads
"operated by Quinzel" on one of the doors.

00:14:55.190 --> 00:14:59.230
Talking of psychiatrists, the author of the
book, "Setting Limits For Your Out of Control

00:14:59.230 --> 00:15:03.690
Child", which Alfred is reading, is none other
than Dr Bartholomew Wolper.

00:15:03.690 --> 00:15:07.600
Dr Wolper appeared in Frank Miller's graphic
novels The Dark Knight Returns as a doctor

00:15:07.600 --> 00:15:11.810
who claimed that Batman's extreme vigilantism
and disregard of criminals' rights was the

00:15:11.810 --> 00:15:13.360
cause of the Joker's insanity.

00:15:13.360 --> 00:15:18.000
Ironically, Wolper met his end at the hands
of the Joker when he tried to prove this live

00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:19.000
on TV.

00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:22.970
And when Batman has to confront the Joker
in a hall of mirrors back at Wayne Manor,

00:15:22.970 --> 00:15:26.750
which the Joker has converted into a theme
park, it's to nod to The Dark Knight Returns

00:15:26.750 --> 00:15:30.850
comic and the showdown between Batman and
the Joker which occurs in a house of mirrors

00:15:30.850 --> 00:15:32.600
at an amusement park.

00:15:32.600 --> 00:15:37.000
Michael Jackson's song Man In The Mirror appears
and forms the basis of numerous gags throughout

00:15:37.000 --> 00:15:38.000
the movie.

00:15:38.000 --> 00:15:41.590
It's interesting that a Michael Jackson track
plays such an important part in the Lego Batman

00:15:41.590 --> 00:15:45.829
Movie as Jackson and Prince, who were both
big Batman fans, were actually supposed to

00:15:45.829 --> 00:15:50.100
collaborate on the music for Tim Burton's
1989 Batman film.

00:15:50.100 --> 00:15:53.900
Lego Batman's favourite movie seems to be
Jerry Maguire and he loves laughing at the

00:15:53.900 --> 00:15:58.360
line "you complete me", which relates to the
theme of Batman finding friendship and family,

00:15:58.360 --> 00:16:01.920
and also to his dysfunctional relationship
with the Joker!

00:16:01.920 --> 00:16:05.960
On top of that, it's also a wink at the Joker's
"you complete me" line to Batman in The Dark

00:16:05.960 --> 00:16:08.630
Knight, which itself was a nod to Jerry Maguire.

00:16:08.630 --> 00:16:13.150
Indeed, Renée Zellweger's famous line, "you
had me at hello", is also parodied at the

00:16:13.150 --> 00:16:17.370
end of Lego Batman when the Joker says to
Batman, "You had me at shut up."

00:16:17.370 --> 00:16:22.100
And the Lego Movie's Infinite Abyss of Nothingness
gets a shout-out when Dr Quivers comes on

00:16:22.100 --> 00:16:27.340
TV and explains how Gotham is built on a bunch
of flimsy plates that are stuck together and

00:16:27.340 --> 00:16:29.250
under which is an infinite abyss.

